---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { ADS_ENABLED, ANALYTICS_TOKEN, CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../config';
const analyticsOn = ANALYTICS_TOKEN.length > 0;
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy – Files Stay on Your Device | HugMyFile"
  description="HugMyFile processes your files locally in your browser and never uploads them. Read what we collect, what we never collect, analytics and ads."
  path="/privacy-policy"
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  lead="The short version: your files never leave your device, and we do not track you."
  updated="October 29, 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Your files</h2>
  <p>
    Every tool on {SITE_NAME} runs inside your web browser. When you choose, drop or paste a file, it is read and processed by your
    own device. <strong>Your files are never uploaded to us or to anyone else.</strong> We do not have a server that receives files,
    we do not store them, and we cannot see them. When you close or reload the page, the files and results in that tab are gone.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some tools need extra building blocks to work, such as PDF rendering code, image encoders, fonts or text-recognition language
    data. Your browser downloads these from our own website when a tool needs them. They are the same for every visitor and
    contain nothing about you or your files.
  </p>

  <h2>2. No accounts, no history</h2>
  <p>
    There are no user accounts, logins or sign-ups. We do not keep a history of what you did, which tools you used or which files
    you processed. The only thing saved in your browser is your light or dark theme choice, and only if you use the theme switch.
    It stays on your device and is never sent to us.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    To understand which pages are useful, we may use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, a privacy-focused service that
    does not use cookies, does not track you across websites and does not build a profile of you. It counts page views and
    collects basic technical information such as the page address, the referring website, your browser type and country. It
    never receives your files.
    {analyticsOn ? ' Analytics is currently turned on.' : ' Analytics is currently turned off.'}
  </p>

  <h2>4. Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    To keep the tools free, we plan to show ads from <strong>Google AdSense</strong>.
    {ADS_ENABLED ? ' Ads are currently turned on.' : ' Ads are not turned on yet.'}
    Once ads are on, Google and its partners may use cookies or similar technologies to show ads and measure them, based on your
    visits to this and other websites. You can learn more in
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>
    and manage personalized ads in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google’s Ad Settings</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland will be asked for their consent through a
    Google-certified consent message before any cookies are used for personalized advertising, and can change their choice at
    any time. Ad code never receives your files, because your files never leave your device.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Hosting and security logs</h2>
  <p>
    Our website is delivered by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical data such as IP addresses to deliver
    pages and protect the site from abuse. We do not use this data to identify you.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Children</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} is made for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
    information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because we do not collect personal data through the tools and do not run accounts, there is usually nothing about you for us
    to access, correct or delete. If you have a question or a request about your privacy, please get in touch.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, we will update this page and the “Last updated” date above.</p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {CONTACT_EMAIL ? (
      <>Email us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</>
    ) : (
      <>See our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Our contact email is coming soon.</>
    )}
  </p>
</PageLayout>
